//
// The entire DDS type vocabulary for SCE Mesh.
//
// One opaque envelope carries every pattern — request, reply, notification,
// fire-and-forget alike — because the service vocabulary lives inside the
// CBOR MeshEnvelope (§mesh-7.5), not in the DDS type system. OMG DDS-RPC
// takes the opposite approach: an IDL interface per service, regenerated
// whenever a service gains an operation. Here, adding an event, a machine,
// or a whole deployment changes nothing in this file, so no generated DDS
// type ever goes stale against a topology.
//
// The cost of that choice is that DDS-native tooling sees octets rather than
// typed fields. That is the correct trade for SCE: the authority on payload
// shape is the SCXML/EventSchema layer, and a second, DDS-specific schema
// would be a second place for it to drift.

module sce_mesh {
    struct Envelope {
        sequence<octet> payload;
    };
};
